{"id":31689,"slug":"cooley-high","title":"Cooley High","year":1975,"country":"United States","duration":107,"spine":1165,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/31689-cooley-high","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/b5eb300bc44bdc8158328e424a77c82f/2I9V8aMWRlz5RhuORsQt31U7gdzTfC_large.jpg","description":"Chicago, 1964: it’s the end of high school for aspiring poet Preach and his best friend, Cochise, and they have a full slate of extracurricular activities: swinging dance parties, late-night joyrides, and the stumbling pursuit of romance. Of course, when you’re a young Black man in America, there’s no guarantee that your coming-of-age story will be free of complications. Director Michael Schultz and screenwriter Eric Monte—who drew on his own experiences growing up in Chicago’s Cabrini-Green housing project—arrived at something truly unique in 1970s cinema with Cooley High: an endearingly funny, tender, and authentic portrait of Black teens striving toward a brighter future, brought to life by a dynamic ensemble cast and set to a heavenly hit parade of Motown classics.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Michael Schultz","slug":"michael-schultz"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Glynn Turman","role":"Preach","slug":"glynn-turman"},{"actor":"Lawrence Hilton-Jacobs","role":"Cochise","slug":"lawrence-hilton-jacobs"},{"actor":"Garrett Morris","role":"Mr. Mason","slug":"garrett-morris"},{"actor":"Cynthia Davis","role":"Brenda","slug":"cynthia-davis"},{"actor":"Corin Rogers","role":"Pooter","slug":"corin-rogers"},{"actor":"Maurice Leon Havis","role":"Willie","slug":"maurice-leon-havis"},{"actor":"Joseph Carter Wilson","role":"Tyrone","slug":"joseph-carter-wilson"},{"actor":"Sherman Smith","role":"Stone","slug":"sherman-smith"},{"actor":"Norman Gibson","role":"Robert","slug":"norman-gibson"},{"actor":"Maurice Marshall","role":"Damon","slug":"maurice-marshall"},{"actor":"Steven Williams","role":"Jimmy Lee","slug":"steven-williams"},{"actor":"Jackie Taylo